===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To perform an action reminiscent of ballet [[dancing]].
#* '''2014''' Rutherford's Vascular Surgery E-Book - Page 1340
#*: Situations that typically require longer iliac limbs than the measurements suggest include extreme iliac tortuosity, “'''ballet'''ing” of the limbs (Endurant and Excluder) (Fig. 90-3), and the need to extend to the external iliac arteries. It these anatomic circumstances, it is prudent to choose a longer length when in doubt.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2016|author=Jacob Russell Dring|title=Endless the Chase
|passage=Unfortunately, he could only sustain so much abuse. Footfalls approached. Kanoa's lips smacked and his jaw hung open. His eyelids fluttered, their underlying gaze '''balleting''' without clarity. He felt beyond sick, and his world spun immensely. A garbled voice of incoherency seemed to be his only link to this realm of consciousness.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2017|author=Num Nums|chapter=A Total Bust a Move|title=The ZhuZhus
|passage=Frankie's obviously going to '''ballet''' her way to the trophy.}}

